  "reconstruction": {
    "output_components": [
      "real",
      "imag"
    ],
    "rule": "Validate sample_values has exactly one key z_index with value in {-2,-1,0,1,2}. If z_index!=0, define R_state,k=expectation(state_k_real), I_state,k=expectation(state_k_imag), s_hadron=+1, s_vacuum=-1. Return Re=sum_state s_state*(R_state,0-I_state,1+I_state,2+R_state,3)/2 and Im=sum_state s_state*(I_state,0+R_state,1-R_state,2+I_state,3)/2. If z_index=0, return Re=expectation(vacuum_z0_Z5)-expectation(hadron_z0_Z5) and Im=0. Identity contributions cancel exactly between the hadron and vacuum coefficients.",
    "terms": [
      {
        "coefficient": "for z_index!=0: Re +1/2; Im 0",
        "recipe_id": "hadron_k0_real"
      },
      {
        "coefficient": "for z_index!=0: Re 0; Im +1/2",
        "recipe_id": "hadron_k0_imag"
